      &lt;/div&gt;               &lt;b class="toggle-caption"&gt;               &lt;svg class="icon icon--info"&gt;&lt;use href="#icon-info"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;               &lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/b&gt;     &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;ol class="edTag"&gt;&lt;li&gt;Muslim pitmasters in Texas are gaining &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/09/06/nx-s1-5927184/american-muslims-are-giving-texas-barbecue-a-halal-makeover" target="_blank"&gt;recognition for their unique halal takes&lt;/a&gt; on the state's iconic barbecue, as Republican leaders target the growing Muslim communities.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Authorities have &lt;a href="https://www.statenews.org/news/2026-09-06/armed-person-reported-to-have-lunged-at-democratic-candidate-for-ohio-governor-injuring-others" target="_blank"&gt;arrested an armed man&lt;/a&gt; who allegedly lunged at Democratic candidate for Ohio governor Amy Acton at the Canfield Fair, injuring several bystanders in the process. (via &lt;a href="https://www.statenews.org/" target="_blank"&gt;Statehouse News Bureau&lt;/a&gt;)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Researchers have published findings that reveal key biological &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/09/04/nx-s1-5954823/profound-autism-proteins-genes-map-treatments" target="_blank"&gt;insights into profound autism&lt;/a&gt; and offer new targets for drug development.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;   &lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;This newsletter was edited by &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/people/859721331/suzanne-nuyen"target="_blank"   &gt;&lt;em&gt;Suzanne Nuyen&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt; &lt;/div&gt;</description>
