 North America                                      &lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;b class="hide-caption"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/p&gt;         &lt;/div&gt;               &lt;b class="toggle-caption"&gt;               &lt;svg class="icon icon--info"&gt;&lt;use href="#icon-info"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;               &lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/b&gt;     &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;ol class="edTag"&gt;&lt;li&gt;Olivia Rodrigo put politics center stage with her inaugural one-day Daisy Chain Fields festival. The event &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/09/02/nx-s1-5953948/olivia-rodrigo-daisy-chain-fields-festival-review" target="_blank"&gt;raised $20 million for 10 organizations&lt;/a&gt;, including the Center for Reproductive Rights and the National Women's Law Center.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Researchers at the University of Vermont, as part of an international team, have &lt;a href="https://www.vermontpublic.org/local-news/2026-09-03/uvm-scientists-helped-uncover-possible-explanation-bat-longevity-cancer" target="_blank"&gt;found how bats avoid disease and live long&lt;/a&gt; lives. Their findings may one day help humans achieve the same. (via &lt;a href="https://www.vermontpublic.org/" target="_blank"&gt;Vermont Public&lt;/a&gt;)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Jurors in Lindsay Clancy's murder trial &lt;a href="https://www.wbur.org/news/2026/09/03/lindsay-clancy-trial-jury-deliberations" target="_blank"&gt;return today to continue deliberations&lt;/a&gt;, after telling the judge for the third time yesterday that they remained deadlocked. A single juror appears to be in disagreement with the others. (via &lt;a href="https://www.wbur.org/" target="_blank"&gt;WBUR&lt;/a&gt;)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;       &lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;This newsletter was edited by &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/people/859721331/suzanne-nuyen"target="_blank"   &gt;&lt;em&gt;Suzanne Nuyen&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt; &lt;/div&gt;</description>
